title op6: a delta whose lost names straddle the split

# Shape four of four for the PENDING set-delta proposal: the residual
# conflict the proposal keeps deliberately.  See op6-split-quiet.tree
# for the gold policy.
#
# Onto un-shares z into its own dnode.  Off-of renames x to aa and z
# to cc, so the delta is lost {x, z} gained {aa, cc} -- and the two
# lost names now sit in DIFFERENT fragments of onto's split.
#
# The gains cannot be partitioned to follow.  Content and position
# evidence cannot say whether aa succeeds x or z, and the document's
# impossibility argument stands: nothing observable distinguishes the
# labels.  So this conflicts, and it should.
#
# Today:                conflict pooling, by the degrade branch --
#                       two lost, two gained, no pairing, attachment
#                       links meeting the split's exclusions.
# Under the proposal:   conflict, by the straddle rule -- the delta's
#                       lost set spans two fragments, so it routes to
#                       neither.
#
# THE VERDICT IS THE SAME AND THE GOLD IS THE SAME.  What differs is
# the reason and the report: today the engine says it could not pair
# two renames, and under the proposal it says a group lost {x, z} and
# gained {aa, cc} across a split, which is a true statement about
# what happened rather than a statement about what the algorithm
# could not do.
#
# That distinction is invisible to this suite, and saying so is the
# point of the fixture.  The gold tier checks the decided tree and
# the conflict kinds; it does not read the report's wording.  A
# fixture cannot tell the difference between the old reason and the
# new one, so if the report text matters -- and for the OP6 defect it
# does, since "at least it fails loudly" was the whole defence -- it
# needs a census-tier or manifest assertion, not a gold section.
# That is a gap in what wave 1 can prove, and it is better on the
# record than discovered later.
#
# CONFIDENCE: the quarantine set is derived by analogy with the
# two-renames/ arm of 6-ambiguous-succession.tree, as in
# op6-delta-within-fragment.tree, and carries the same caveat.

tree base
  1-1: /
    2-100: shared/
      10-100: x = v0
      10-100: y
      10-100: z

tree onto
  1-1: /
    2-100: shared/
      10-100: x = v0
      10-100: y
      30-200: z = v0

tree offof
  1-1: /
    2-100: shared/
      10-100: aa = v0
      10-100: cc
      10-100: y

# --- expected result, worked by hand 2026-08-31 ---
expect conflict pooling
expect quarantined /shared/x
expect quarantined /shared/y
expect quarantined /shared/z

tree expected
  1-1: /
    2-100: shared
      10-100: x = v0
      10-100: y
      30-200: z = v0
